00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.170
So, a gel

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.463
is made of agarose,

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.390
basically it's a polymer.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:46.840
So it's made up of several
units and it's like jello.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.163
So you watch, I can poke it.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:55.170
And like, it's quite a hard
one, it's a high percentage.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:59.940
And we talk about gels as a
percent of the total volume.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:03.360
And we have these little cones in here

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.380
that lets us make wells where
we can load our samples.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.570
So I'm just pulling out the cone

00:05:11.257 --> 00:05:13.470
and then we'll take it
out of this little tray

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.353
where we make it, one second.

00:05:20.059 --> 00:05:21.873
And I can get this out with.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:29.773
So sorry y'all, I'm gonna put
you like that for a second.

00:05:29.773 --> 00:05:30.606
Yeah.

00:05:32.333 --> 00:05:35.343
Yeah, we have this fun panel,
looks like a piece of jello.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:41.840
And in this you have a
chemical called indium bromide.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:45.310
Basically it stains DNA.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.173
So when we put DNA in these wells,

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.230
we'll be able to see it by

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.960
imaging.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.780
So to start, we're gonna
actually walk with our gel

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:04.593
to the box where we put
it in for electrophoresis.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.350
We use electricity to move the DNA.

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:12.340
So I'm not sure if you all know,

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.080
the charge of DNA is negative

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:18.263
because of the phosphate backbones.

00:06:19.719 --> 00:06:21.860
I'm gonna leave you over here for a second

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.183
while I pour some stuff.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.910
Yeah, the phosphate backbone
of DNA makes it negative.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:31.743
So,

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:37.010
negative charges like
should be really far away

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:38.793
from other negative charges.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.883
Negative charges are
attracted to positives.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.580
The whole positive attract kind of thing.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.603
I actually can't see if we can see this.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.517
So we put the gel in

00:06:52.517 --> 00:06:57.300
and we add what's essentially
salty water around it

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.680
so that the electricity can be conducted

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.773
because regular water isn't
that good of a conductor.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:11.330
So on the back side, we'll
apply a negative charge.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.090
And ours actually even has a little,

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:17.193
it's hard to see, negative sign
there, so you don't forget.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:21.260
And on the red side, we
have a positive charge

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:25.053
and we'll put DNA right at
the top in these little wells.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:30.620
And negative DNA will move
away from the negative well,

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:31.583
and it will,

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:33.813
sorry.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:38.230
And it'll move down to the positive well.

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:40.710
And you can think of it kind of like

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.680
you're trying to move in a sea of people.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:48.030
If you are like really,
really tall at a concert,

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.930
it can be really hard to move
when there's a lot of people.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.120
But if you're really short at a concert,

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:58.420
you can move really easily
through a tight group of people.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.780
And it's the same thing with the DNA.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.580
If the DNA is really big in size,

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.333
it has trouble moving through the agarose,

00:08:06.333 --> 00:08:08.800
so it'll get stuck up at the top.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.050
But the really small pieces
can move quite easily,

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.083
so it'll go down.

