00:29:11.200 --> 00:29:14.890
So the enzyme doesn't know
what you're trying to amplify,

00:29:14.890 --> 00:29:18.130
it just knows, oh, look, there's DNA here.

00:29:18.130 --> 00:29:19.850
So you give it a little direction.

00:29:19.850 --> 00:29:24.170
You give it a primer that
just like these pieces

00:29:25.120 --> 00:29:25.953
bind.

00:29:27.100 --> 00:29:27.933
So,

00:29:29.810 --> 00:29:31.510
now they're a little piece of DNA,

00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:38.180
that binds here and then has this opening.

00:29:38.180 --> 00:29:43.010
So you give it a little
headstart of priming

00:29:43.010 --> 00:29:47.230
and then it will allow the
polymerase to keep reading

00:29:47.230 --> 00:29:50.570
and keep attaching nucleotides.

00:29:50.570 --> 00:29:53.440
So the polymerase will go through and say,

00:29:53.440 --> 00:29:56.000
ah, yes what pairs with a C?

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:58.190
And it'll go through all
the different nucleotides

00:29:58.190 --> 00:30:02.833
and it'll say cheek, and
it'll catalyze that reaction.

00:30:03.925 --> 00:30:06.313
It'll go all the way through and then,

00:30:09.030 --> 00:30:10.830
you'll make your whole piece

00:30:11.740 --> 00:30:14.680
and you'll change the temperature
and you'll start again

00:30:14.680 --> 00:30:16.620
'cause it's a chain reaction.

00:30:16.620 --> 00:30:21.390
Whereas the product of each
cycle becomes the template,

00:30:21.390 --> 00:30:24.610
the starting DNA for the next cycle.

00:30:24.610 --> 00:30:27.773
So you get many, many
more pieces over and over.

00:30:30.810 --> 00:30:33.980
And I've kind of written
out way you do that,

00:30:33.980 --> 00:30:37.140
is we take one piece of DNA,

00:30:37.140 --> 00:30:39.800
we get it really hot to denature it,

00:30:39.800 --> 00:30:41.543
break the two strands apart.

00:30:42.520 --> 00:30:44.800
And then when the primers match up

00:30:44.800 --> 00:30:49.740
with their complimentary
basis, that's called annealing.

00:30:49.740 --> 00:30:53.080
And that happens at a
slightly lower temperature.

00:30:53.080 --> 00:30:54.580
This will actually depend on

00:30:54.580 --> 00:30:57.860
the individual nucleotide sequences,

00:30:57.860 --> 00:30:59.820
which are these guys right here.

