00:31:05.730 --> 00:31:07.880
You get a lower temperature

00:31:07.880 --> 00:31:11.663
to kind of help the primer
find its matching spot.

00:31:13.270 --> 00:31:17.380
Then you'll go through
extension or elongation

00:31:17.380 --> 00:31:20.920
where you add in all of the nucleotides,

00:31:20.920 --> 00:31:23.953
this is your actual
amplification reaction.

00:31:25.240 --> 00:31:30.240
And then you do this again and
again like 25 to 30 cycles.

00:31:31.330 --> 00:31:34.110
And you have a ton of product,

