00:34:11.190 --> 00:34:14.340
Primers bind during the annealing stage.

00:34:14.340 --> 00:34:16.803
They come together and
match with the template.

00:34:17.961 --> 00:34:22.757
Denaturing which was when we
broke the two strands apart.

00:34:24.740 --> 00:34:27.710
Denature is any time you
break apart something.

00:34:27.710 --> 00:34:30.770
So you can also denature a protein,

00:34:30.770 --> 00:34:34.470
break it up into its amino acid monomers.

00:34:34.470 --> 00:34:38.770
When you break apart DNA, you apply heat

00:34:38.770 --> 00:34:41.260
and break it up into the strands.

00:34:41.260 --> 00:34:44.100
The nucleotides are unmatched

00:34:44.100 --> 00:34:48.810
And the extension step
was where we added in

00:34:48.810 --> 00:34:52.200
our new nucleotides to
make that amplification.

00:34:52.200 --> 00:34:55.360
So after our primer had bound

00:34:55.360 --> 00:34:58.840
when we added in each
individual nucleotides

00:34:58.840 --> 00:35:03.390
