00:36:31.060 --> 00:36:33.970
Exactly, gel electrophoresis,

00:36:33.970 --> 00:36:38.450
that agarose gel separates DNA by size.

00:36:38.450 --> 00:36:40.450
I see polarity may have tripped you up

00:36:40.450 --> 00:36:43.910
because we talked a lot about
the charge and the electricity

00:36:44.890 --> 00:36:49.450
but that charge just
helps you move the DNA.

00:36:49.450 --> 00:36:52.850
So DNA because of that phosphate backbone

00:36:52.850 --> 00:36:56.897
is negative by putting a
negative charge at the top

00:36:56.897 --> 00:36:59.370
and a positive charge at the bottom,

00:36:59.370 --> 00:37:04.150
you forced the DNA to move
away from the negative charge.

00:37:04.150 --> 00:37:08.700
And then as it's moving big
pieces get stuck in the agarose,

00:37:08.700 --> 00:37:11.830
small pieces slide through quite easily.

00:37:11.830 --> 00:37:15.350
So by applying an electric charge,

00:37:15.350 --> 00:37:18.033
you are able to separate
your pieces by size.

