is that his first name?

00:51:02.720 --> 00:51:03.690
I'm not sure.

00:51:03.690 --> 00:51:07.853
Oh, Watson and Crick discovered
this double helix structure.

00:51:08.700 --> 00:51:10.770
And we actually call these base pairs

00:51:10.770 --> 00:51:12.920
Watson and Crick pairing

00:51:12.920 --> 00:51:15.310
because they figured out
that these two go together

00:51:15.310 --> 00:51:16.800
and it makes the shape

00:51:16.800 --> 00:51:20.210
and this like revolutionized
the world of biology.

00:51:20.210 --> 00:51:24.210
But what we don't usually talk
about is the way they knew

00:51:24.210 --> 00:51:29.210
that it was the structure was
because this female scientist

00:51:29.340 --> 00:51:32.180
called Roslyn Franklin had done

00:51:33.080 --> 00:51:35.200
x-ray crystallography.

00:51:35.200 --> 00:51:37.700
Basically she took this molecule

00:51:37.700 --> 00:51:42.310
like down the middle like this
and shot x-rays through it

00:51:42.310 --> 00:51:44.523
and it made this pattern.

00:51:46.317 --> 00:51:47.730
You can see how it's
kind of like the spokes

00:51:47.730 --> 00:51:48.883
than the outside.

00:51:49.720 --> 00:51:52.280
And she said, well, one
of the ways you could get

00:51:52.280 --> 00:51:55.633
that pattern is with a double helix.

00:51:55.633 --> 00:51:59.450
And her data helped Watson
and Crick figure out

00:51:59.450 --> 00:52:00.373
that structure.

